\(O(\log n)\): Logarithmic
def binary_search(arr, target):
    lo, hi = 0, len(arr) - 1
    while lo &lt;= hi:
        mid = (lo + hi) // 2
        if arr[mid] == target:
            return mid
        elif arr[mid] &lt; target:
            lo = mid + 1
        else:
            hi = mid - 1
    return -1

“Halving at each step. \(\log_2(1 \text{ billion}) \approx 30\).”
“Worst case: target not in array. We halve until the range is empty → \(\Theta(\log n)\).”
